            <ArticleTitle>[Posterior spinal cord neurostimulation in lumbar radiculitis pain. Apropos of 14 cases].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>137-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In 14 patients, spinal cord stimulation in lumbar radiculopathy follow multiple exploration or iterative surgery. For 10 out of this 14 patients treatment was successful; pain relief lasted a mean time of 12.7 months in 9 out of them.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
